## Review Fix

The review identified one important gap: qualification did not carry or verify the authenticated
friction/scenario-grid identity shared by baseline and candidate. The campaign plan was updated
only in the directly affected qualification boundary:

- `QualificationAttemptCommitmentV5` now carries `scenario_grid_ref`.
- Qualification attempt construction requires the immutable authenticated scenario-grid reference
  and fails closed unless it matches the attempt, baseline evidence, and candidate evidence.
- Qualification assertions and outcome verification explicitly require the same shared
  friction/scenario-grid identity, matching the confirmation comparison boundary.

Focused check:

```powershell
$text=Get-Content -Raw 'docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-04-pit-optimizer-v5-campaign.md'
foreach ($needle in @('scenario_grid_ref','friction/scenario-grid identity','equal for the attempt, baseline, and candidate','same-panel V5 baseline evaluated under the exact shared authenticated')) { if ($text -notmatch [regex]::Escape($needle)) { throw "missing: $needle" } }
```

Result: `focused qualification consistency checks: PASS`.

Fix commit:

```text
0707f4c docs: bind qualification scenario identity
```

Commit hooks passed the applicable whitespace, EOF, merge-conflict, Ruff/YAML gating checks
(Ruff and YAML skipped because no applicable files were present). No tests, provider calls,
Docker/replay, or external writes were performed.

## Review Fix Round 2

The second review found that the prior fix had placed `scenario_grid_ref` only on
`ConfirmationAttemptCommitmentV5`, while qualification prose claimed the field existed there too.
The minimal correction adds exactly one `scenario_grid_ref: ArtifactRefV5` field to
`QualificationAttemptCommitmentV5`; the confirmation field remains intentional. Qualification
construction/checklist/equality verification now consistently refers to that authenticated shared
baseline/candidate friction scenario-grid identity.

Focused read-only check:

```powershell
$text=Get-Content -Raw 'docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-04-pit-optimizer-v5-campaign.md'
$confirmation=[regex]::Match($text,'(?s)class ConfirmationAttemptCommitmentV5:.*?(?=\n@dataclass)').Value
$qualification=[regex]::Match($text,'(?s)class QualificationAttemptCommitmentV5:.*?(?=\n@dataclass)').Value
```

Result: `round-2 focused qualification checks: PASS` — both commitment classes contain exactly one
`scenario_grid_ref: ArtifactRefV5`, and qualification equality-verification prose is present.

Round-2 fix commit:

```text
582dfca docs: bind qualification scenario grid
```

No tests, provider calls, Docker/replay, or external writes were performed.
